   "#c9a227"
  ],
  "pitch": "The dead of Wend have come back to finish their chores, and nobody in the village wants you to stop them.",
  "about": [
   "Forty years ago they dammed the river and drowned the old village, church and all. Now the bell is ringing down there. The first dead man came home on a Tuesday, mended a fence he had promised to mend, and sat down by the fire. His widow gave him soup. He cannot eat it. She gives it to him every night.",
   "Bells Under Wend is a ghost story about people who are not afraid of the ghosts. The heroes must find who is ringing the bell, what he wants with so many willing hands, and whether it is a mercy to stop him."
  ],
  "patron": [
   "Hanne Rook",
   "constable of Wend, who buried her brother twice"
