  "pitch": "A dwarf-hold barred its doors three winters ago. Every evening a small voice answers the knock, and will not let anyone in.",
  "about": [
   "Karag Dun has not paid toll, sold iron or opened its gate in three years. Smoke still rises. Somebody still answers the door. The grown-ups, says the voice, are busy.",
   "The Barred Hold is an adventure about getting in, and then about what has been holding the place together. There are machines to reason with, a parliament with a height limit, and, a long way down, a market where the only coin is your own name."
  ],
  "patron": [
