  "pitch": "Every harvest the village crowns a King for a day. This year he went up into the wood, and the wood has sent him back with horns.",
  "about": [
   "Hazelmere has kept the bargain for three hundred years: one day in the year a man wears the straw crown, is feasted, is chased laughing to the edge of the trees, and comes home to bed. Nobody remembers what it was for. The wood does.",
   "A Crown of Antlers is a campaign of forests, laws and consequences. The heroes will be hunted, and will learn the rules; and at the end of it someone has to wear the crown."
  ],
